# For each word the note is shown, and a word with `+` writes over it: the first round reads the note as it was, and a
# later round writes on it, though the write stands above the read in the loop. Read, then written: both.

route loopnote.run
step run/for word in sys.argv[1:]                           # the words the human typed, each kept as `word`
line entry > run call
line entry > run/for word in sys.argv[1:] call             # the command line is the entry's
line run/for word in sys.argv[1:] > _·word@run/for word in sys.argv[1:] value
line _·word@run/for word in sys.argv[1:] > run value   # `word.startswith(..)`, `NOTE.write_text(word)`
home _·word@run/for word in sys.argv[1:] run
line File(data/note.txt) > run own
line run > File(data/note.txt) own
line run > Screen own

side entry left
side File(data/note.txt) both
side Screen right
